<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alberto Scotti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1318</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alberto <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scoti">Scotti</a> was a Guelph nobleman and merchant who made himself lord of Piacenza in 1290. He was driven out and returned several times amid struggles with the Visconti and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> lords, and his career illustrates the passage of Italian communes into signorie ruled by single families.</p></div>
